        <item>
            <title>3.7.0</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 16:55:00 +0900</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/Saqoosha/Canopy</link>
            <sparkle:version>172</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>3.7.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[### Features
- Claude Code extension updates now install automatically, with no restart. New sessions use the new extension; sessions already running keep their version. A macOS notification tells you when an update is installed, and the banner offers Retry if an install fails.

### Changes
- The sidebar's 5-hour and weekly usage bars are now colored by pace: gray when usage is on or behind the time elapsed in the window, orange when it is running ahead, and red when it is ahead and at 90% or more, or the quota is used up. Per-model rows keep the previous percentage thresholds.
- The pace marker on those bars is wider and no longer clipped, so it is easier to spot.
- The "Restart Now" button and the Save and Restart prompt are gone, since extension updates no longer need a restart.

### Bug Fixes
- The Settings window no longer flashes at the wrong size when first opened after launch.
]]></description>
